{
  "_about": "Ground truth for the ARSI anomaly benchmark: ONE protocol over every labelled frame we have, five cameras of two trams. Each case pairs an inspection image with the clean reference it is diffed against (a key of 'references'), a frame-level has_anomaly label (the primary binary metric) and zero or more instances. instances = OBJECT-level ground truth: one entry per real anomaly, with its type and a bounding box in the pixel space of THAT case's reference (real = 1920x1080, variant = 1672x941, the four 39T cameras = 1280x720; frames of a different size are uniformly resized onto their reference). Boxes are intentionally generous: a detected instance = any kept region overlapping it. Types: object = forgotten object, graffiti, damage = vandalism/torn seat, litter = trash on the floor. People are NOT instances (a kept box on a person is a false positive). source: real = a frame from the actual camera, gpt = an AI-inpainted test image on the real scene, variant = a second synthetic scene with its own reference, self = a reference diffed against itself.\n\nTRAM 1762, camera 'real' + the synthetic 'variant' scene (July, 29 cases, 45 instances). Anomalous: 6 real CCTV frames (forgotten objects, one with a real seated person) + 10 AI-inpainted frames + 1 variant scene. Clean: reference-vs-self x2, a clean AI frame, 4 same-session empty frames and 5 CROSS-SESSION empty frames (v2/v3/v4 against the v1 reference), which are the deployment-realistic negatives: different exposure, onboard-display content changes, one walking person. Known benign cross-session differences on this camera: display content (bottom right), an equipment bag at the very bottom edge present in BOTH sessions, global exposure drift.\n\nTRAM 39T, cameras 39T-cam52..55 (recorded 2026-08-11, built 2026-08-16 by tools/build_39T_benchmark.py, 21 cases, 24 instances). Every image is the t=60 s frame of its video, masked with that camera's own mask, so it is exactly what the pipeline sees. Each camera is its own reference: itself during moment 08-55-37, verified empty on all 15 interior cameras. The other moments are separate runs of the line, so a negative here is a cross-session negative: different sun, different position on the track. These labels were drafted by Claude, by eye, never by running our own localizer, and each instance was confirmed by comparing the same crop in the reference and in the inspection frame; that test rejected two candidates (a seat cover present in both frames, a sunlit floor patch). Correct them in the Studio's Benchmark screen.",
  "name": "ARSI benchmark: trams 1762 and 39T, 5 cameras",
